      "id": "e1",
      "title": "Numbers 20 to 1000 and beyond",
      "body": "After 20 the system is regular up to 69. Then it changes: French counts 70 as sixty-ten, 80 as four-twenties, and 90 as four-twenties-ten. This is true in both France and Québec. (Belgium and Switzerland use septante and nonante, so you may hear these from time to time, but you do not need to say them.)"
    },
