    {
      "type": "explain",
      "id": "e2",
      "title": "Numbers 20 to 1000 and beyond",
      "body": "• et un is used for 21, 31, 41, 51, 61 and 71 (vingt et un, soixante et onze), but not for 81 and 91 (quatre-vingt-un, quatre-vingt-onze).\n• quatre-vingts takes an s only when nothing follows (80). With another number, no s: quatre-vingt-deux. The same for cent: deux cents, but deux cent trois.\n• mille never takes an s. Trois mille (3000)."
    },
